# Environment Variables Template

Copy this file to each directory and rename to `.env`, then fill in your values.

## Frontend (.env in /frontend)

```
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api
VITE_APP_NAME=NyaySathi
```

## Backend (.env in /backend)

```
# Server Configuration
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development

# Supabase Configuration
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# JWT Configuration
JWT_SECRET=generate_a_random_string_here_using_openssl_rand_-base64_32

# AI Service Configuration
PYTHON_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Email Configuration (optional)
EMAIL_SERVICE=gmail
EMAIL_USER=your_email@gmail.com
EMAIL_PASSWORD=your_app_password
EMAIL_FROM=noreply@nyaysathi.com

# Logging
LOG_LEVEL=info
```

## AI Service (.env in /ai-service)

```
# OpenAI Configuration
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your_openai_api_key_here

# Supabase Configuration
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# API Configuration
API_HOST=0.0.0.0
API_PORT=8000

# Debug Mode
DEBUG=False
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
```

## Root (.env in project root for docker-compose)

```
# All settings from backend, frontend, and ai-service combined
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api
VITE_APP_NAME=NyaySathi

PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development

SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

JWT_SECRET=generate_a_random_string_here

PYTHON_SERVICE_URL=http://ai-service:8000

OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your_openai_api_key_here

API_HOST=0.0.0.0
API_PORT=8000

DEBUG=False
LOG_LEVEL=info
```

## How to Generate Values

### JWT_SECRET (Backend)
```bash
openssl rand -base64 32
```

### SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
1. Go to [supabase.com](https://supabase.com)
2. Create or select a project
3. Go to Settings > API
4. Copy Project URL and Anon Key

### OPENAI_API_KEY
1. Go to [platform.openai.com](https://platform.openai.com)
2. Login to your account
3. Go to API Keys
4. Create a new secret key
5. Copy it immediately (it won't be shown again)

### EMAIL_PASSWORD (Gmail App Password)
1. Enable 2-Factor Authentication on Gmail account
2. Go to [myaccount.google.com/apppasswords](https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords)
3. Select Mail and Windows Computer (or your device)
4. Generate app password
5. Use the password (remove spaces)

## Security Notes

⚠️ **Never commit `.env` files to git!**
- `.env` files are added to `.gitignore`
- Never share API keys or secrets
- Rotate keys regularly
- Use different keys for development and production
- Store secrets securely (use secret management in production)
